# Allowlist model, not a denylist.
#
# vsce keeps a file when no ignore pattern matches it OR when a negated (`!`)
# pattern matches it — negation always wins. Ignoring `**` first therefore makes
# the VSIX contents a closed set: anything not re-included below is excluded, so
# a new file or a new directory in the repository root stays out of the package
# by default instead of shipping silently.
#
# `pnpm run check:vsce` (src/tools/vsixPolicy.ts) re-verifies the package that
# was actually produced against the same allowlist, so this file and the
# verifier must always be changed together.
**

# Extension manifest and the marketplace-facing documents.
!package.json
!package.nls.json
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!LICENSE

# Marketplace icon and Activity Bar icon referenced from package.json.
!resources/icon.png
!resources/icon.svg

# README screenshots. Only *.png — no .gitkeep, no SCREENSHOTS.md.
!images/*.png

# Bundled extension code. Only *.cjs directly inside out/ is re-included: that
# is the tsdown/rolldown bundle — `out/extension.cjs` plus chunk files whose
# names carry a build-dependent content hash. Everything else the build or the
# test compile drops into out/ stays excluded, notably out/**/*.map,
# out/test/**/*.js and any other tsc output.
!out/*.cjs
